"def reference(vectors):\n    A, B, C = 0, 1, 2\n    state = A\n    out = []\n    for row in vectors:\n        areset = int(row.get('areset', 0))\n        x = int(row.get('x', 0))\n        if areset:\n            state = A\n        else:\n            if state == A:\n                state = B if x else A\n            elif state == B:\n                state = C if x else B\n            else:\n                state = C if x else B\n        out.append({'z': 1 if state == B else 0})\n    return out\n"
